# Vivado drops these wherever it's invoked from, regardless of project
# directory -- catch them repo-wide rather than per-subdirectory.
.Xil/
retry_open_fs.log
webtalk*
*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str

# Per-machine tool locations (see hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/toolchain.sh)
toolchain.local

# WiFi credentials for the CM4 miner -- keep the PSK out of the repo.
# Ships as a template; fill it in locally or on the running board.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/linux/overlay/etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant-wlan0.conf
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/gen/

# Stray tool output dropped in the REPO ROOT by scripts invoked from here,
# rather than from the directory that owns them. Named specifically rather
# than as a blanket *.log, so a log someone deliberately commits still shows up.
n_*.log
build_*.log

# openXC7 build artefacts. All regenerable from the committed scripts, and all
# large: out_*/ holds netlists (60-90 MB each), FASMs (63 MB) and bitstreams
# (11 MB); seedrun/ holds a route log per seed.
#
# Ignored primarily to keep `git status` legible. With ~70 untracked artefacts
# in the way, a genuinely modified tracked file does not stand out -- a broken
# hdl/odocrypt/encrypt.v sat in the working tree for a day precisely because it
# was one line among that noise.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/out_*/
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/seedrun/
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/*.console
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/.pid_*
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/.done_*
